+  // NV-DXVK start: R13 managed texture memory
+  //
+  // Static managed 2D textures (patch 0022's class) keep their data in exactly one place when
+  // the policy asks for it: the CPU copy (m_buffers) goes once the image holds the data and the
+  // texture has not been locked for a while; a later lock reads the subresource back from the
+  // GPU first. While those textures hold more GPU memory than the budget, images not drawn for
+  // a while are released, least recently used first. Their data stays (read back first if
+  // only the GPU had it) and every subresource is marked for upload, so the next use creates
+  // the image again through patch 0022's path with the hash it had. The renderer may still
+  // hold a released image (cached or anti-culled instances); markApplicationReleased lets the
+  // texture cache free it once no instance samples it, which is when its memory goes.
+  void D3D9DeviceEx::InitManagedTextureMemory() {
+    uint64_t vram = 0;
+    const VkPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties memory = m_dxvkDevice->adapter()->memoryProperties();
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < memory.memoryHeapCount; i++) {
